            'Think of `diff` as the slope of a terrain: `arr[i] = arr[i-1] + diff[i]`, meaning `arr` is the prefix sum of `diff`. Adding `v` at `l` raises the running total by `v` from `l` onward; subtracting `v` at `r+1` brings it back down exactly after `r`. So the running total equals the old value plus `v` on `[l, r]`, and equals the old value everywhere else.',
