            '',
            '## Why It Works (invariant)',
            '',
            'Transposing swaps `a[i][j]` with `a[j][i]` for every `j > i`, so the main diagonal never moves and every off-diagonal pair is exchanged exactly once — the matrix becomes its mirror image across the diagonal. Reversing each row maps column `j` to column `n-1-j`; composing both transforms maps cell `(i, j)` to `(j, n-1-i)`, which is exactly the 90° clockwise rotation.',
