            '1. **Rectangular matrices** — transpose is only in-place for square `n x n`; otherwise build a new `n x m` matrix.',
            '2. **Single row / column** — `n = 1`; transpose and reverse are no-ops.',
            '3. **Empty matrix** — guard before indexing `a[0]`.',
            '4. **1x1 matrix** — rotation leaves it unchanged; loops do not run.',
            '',
            '## Common Mistakes',
            '',
            '- **Transposing with `j < n` instead of `j > i`** — you swap each pair twice and undo the transpose.',
            '- **Out-of-bounds neighbour access** — always bounds-check before reading `a[ni][nj]`.',
            '- **Reading rows vs columns wrongly** — remember `a[i][j]`: row first, column second.',
            '- **Rotating a non-square matrix in place** — only square matrices can rotate in place.',
            '',
            '## Applications',
