            '## Why It Works (invariant)',
            '',
            'After the sort, suppose the sweep has fully merged the prefix `a[0..i-1]` into `res`. The invariant: `res` is sorted, its intervals are mutually disjoint, and `res.back()[1]` is the farthest end reached by any interval in that prefix. For the next interval `a[i]` — the smallest remaining start — if `a[i][0] > res.back()[1]` then it cannot touch any earlier interval (all of them end at or before the running end), so it must open a new block. Otherwise it touches the running block, and only its end can matter, so taking the `max` keeps the block minimal. By induction the final `res` is exactly the merge of all intervals.',
