            '',
            '## Why It Works (invariant)',
            '',
            'Throughout the loop the array holds four contiguous zones: positions `0..lo-1` contain 0s, `lo..mid-1` contain 1s, `mid..hi` are unseen, and `hi+1..n-1` contain 2s. Each iteration reads the *first unseen* element `a[mid]` and places it correctly: a 0 swaps with the first 1 (growing the 0 zone and shrinking the unseen zone), a 1 just advances `mid`, and a 2 swaps with the last unseen slot and shrinks `hi` — note `mid` then stays put because the incoming element is still unseen. The invariant holds after every step, the unseen zone shrinks each iteration, and when `mid > hi` it is empty, so all values are grouped in order.',
            '',
            '## Complexity',
            '',
            '| Aspect | Value | Why |',
            '|---|---|---|',
            '| Time | **O(n)** | Every element is visited a constant number of times |',
            '| Space | **O(1)** | Only three pointer variables |',
            '| Swaps | **≤ n** | At most one swap per non-1 element |',
            '',
            '## Variants',
            '',
            '| Variant | Twist | Approach |',
            '|---|---|---|',
            '| Three-way quicksort | partition around a pivot with duplicate keys | same loop, pivot is the "1" |',
            '| Negative / zero / positive | group three value classes in one pass | identical, relabel the groups |',
            '| Four or more groups | more than three colours | counting sort or stable partition |',
            '| Move zeroes to the end | two groups, preserve order | one swap-free pass or stable partition |',
            '',
            '## Edge Cases',
            '',
            '1. **All one value** — e.g. all 2s: every step swaps with itself and `hi` shrinks; correct, and `mid` never passes a misplaced value.',
            '2. **Already sorted** — the loop only advances `mid`; no swaps occur.',
            '3. **Two colours only** — reduces to a two-way partition.',
            '4. **Empty or single element** — the `mid <= hi` test fails immediately (or runs once).',
            '5. **Long runs of 2s** — each takes one swap and `hi` shrinks; still O(n).',
            '',
            '## Common Mistakes',
            '',
            '- **Advancing `mid` on the 2 branch** — the swapped-in value from `hi` is unseen and would be skipped, corrupting the partition.',
            '- **Using `mid < hi` instead of `mid <= hi`** — the last unseen element (when `mid == hi`) is never processed.',
            '- **Growing `hi` or shrinking `lo` the wrong way** — `lo` moves right, `hi` moves left.',
            '- **Swapping the 1 branch** — 1s are already in the correct zone; swapping breaks the invariant.',
            '- **Off-by-one in zone boundaries** — remember `lo..mid-1` holds 1s, not `lo..mid`.',
            '',
            '## Applications',
            '',
            '- **Sort colors** — the classic LeetCode 75 problem this algorithm is named for.',
            '- **3-way quicksort partitioning** — Dijkstra partition makes quicksort fast on arrays with many duplicates.',
            '- **Partitioning three classes** — negative/zero/positive, old/new/duplicate, allow/deny/unknown.',
            '- **Counting-free grouping** — one pass and constant space when there are exactly three buckets.',
