            '> Reach for it when a problem asks for a "minimum maximum" or "maximum minimum" and a simple feasibility check exists. If you can answer "can we do it with value x?" in O(F), the total is O(F · log R) — often the intended solution.',
            '',
            '## Classic Problems',
            '',
            '| Problem | Answer you search | Feasibility check |',
            '|---|---|---|',
            '| Split array largest sum (LC 410) | largest part sum | can split into ≤ k parts each ≤ x |',
            '| Koko eating bananas (LC 875) | bananas per hour | can finish all piles within h hours |',
            '| Capacity to ship packages (LC 1011) | daily capacity | ships all packages within d days |',
            '| Aggressive cows / magnetic force | minimum distance | can place k balls ≥ d apart |',
            '| Median of two sorted arrays | the k-th element | are enough elements ≤ x |',
            '| Peak in a mountain array | the index | compare mid with its neighbours |',
            '',
            '## Edge Cases',
            '',
