            '## Prefix Sum',
            '',
            'Precompute running totals so any subarray sum becomes one subtraction: `sum(i..j) = p[j] - p[i-1]`. Build it in O(n), answer in O(1).',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: prefixsum',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int a[] = {2, 3, 5, 1};',
            '    int n = 4;',
            '    int p[4];',
            '    p[0] = a[0];',
            '    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) p[i] = p[i - 1] + a[i];',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) printf("%d ", p[i]);',
            '    printf("\\n");',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## The input array. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##4## The array length. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## The prefix array has the same length. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##6## The first prefix is the first element. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##7## Each prefix reuses the previous total. [for]({c:for})',
            '##8## Prints every prefix sum. [for]({c:for})',
            '##10## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: prefixsum',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    vector<int> a = {2, 3, 5, 1};',
            '    int n = a.size();',
            '    vector<int> p(n);',
            '    p[0] = a[0];',
            '    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) p[i] = p[i - 1] + a[i];',
            '    for (int x : p) cout << x << " ";',
            '    cout << "\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##5## `size()` counts the elements. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##6## The prefix array has the same length. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##7## The first prefix is the first element. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##8## Each prefix reuses the previous total. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/for)',
            '##9## Prints every prefix sum. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/range-for)',
            '##11## Success exit. [return](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return)',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: java',
            'group: prefixsum',
            'import java.util.*;',
            'public class Main {',
            '    public static void main(String[] args) {',
            '        int[] a = {2, 3, 5, 1};',
            '        int n = a.length;',
            '        int[] p = new int[n];',
            '        p[0] = a[0];',
            '        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) p[i] = p[i - 1] + a[i];',
            '        for (int x : p) System.out.print(x + " ");',
            '        System.out.println();',
            '    }',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the `java.util` package. [import]({java:import})',
            '##2## In Java every function lives inside a class. [class]({java:class})',
            '##3## `main` is where execution starts. [main]({java:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [Arrays](https://www.w3schools.com/java/java_arrays.asp)',
            '##5## `length` gives the array size. [Variables](https://www.w3schools.com/java/java_variables.asp)',
            '##6## The prefix array has the same length. [Arrays](https://www.w3schools.com/java/java_arrays.asp)',
            '##7## The first prefix is the first element. [Arrays](https://www.w3schools.com/java/java_arrays.asp)',
            '##8## Each prefix reuses the previous total. [for]({java:for})',
            '##9## Prints every prefix sum. [for]({java:for})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: python',
            'group: prefixsum',
            'def main():',
            '    a = [2, 3, 5, 1]',
            '    p = [a[0]]',
            '    for i in range(1, len(a)):',
            '        p.append(p[-1] + a[i])',
            '    print(" ".join(map(str, p)))',
            '',
            'if __name__ == "__main__":',
            '    main()',
            '---',
            '##1## Defines the main function. [def]({python:def})',
            '##2## The input array. [list]({python:list})',
            '##3## The first prefix is the first element. [list]({python:list})',
            '##4## Start from the second element. [range]({python:range})',
            '##5## Each prefix reuses the previous total. [append]({python:append})',
            '##6## Prints every prefix sum. [print]({python:print})',
            '##8## Only runs when executed directly, not imported. [main]({python:main})',
            '##9## Calls `main()` so the program runs. [main]({python:main})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: dart',
            'group: prefixsum',
            'void main() {',
            '  var a = [2, 3, 5, 1];',
            '  var p = <int>[a[0]];',
            '  for (var i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {',
            '    p.add(p.last + a[i]);',
            '  }',
            '  print(p.join(\' \'));',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Top-level entry point of a Dart program. [main]({dart:main})',
            '##2## The input array. [List]({dart:List})',
            '##3## The first prefix is the first element. [List]({dart:List})',
            '##4## Start from the second element. [for]({dart:for})',
            '##5## Each prefix reuses the previous total. [add]({dart:add})',
            '##7## Prints every prefix sum. [print]({dart:print})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~io',
            'input: a = [2, 3, 5, 1]',
            'output:',
            '2 5 10 11',
            '~~~',
            '',
