            '',
            '## Difference Array',
            '',
            'Apply many range-additions in O(n) total: record each range\'s start (+v) and end (-v) in a diff array, then one prefix pass rebuilds the array.',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: diffarray',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int n = 5;',
            '    int d[6] = {0};',
            '    d[1] += 3; d[4] -= 3;',
            '    d[2] += 2; d[5] -= 2;',
            '    int cur = 0;',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {',
            '        cur += d[i];',
            '        printf("%d ", cur);',
            '    }',
            '    printf("\\n");',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## Array of 5 positions. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##4## Diff array with one extra slot for the ending `-v`. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##5## Range [1,3]: +3 at 1, -3 right after the range. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##6## Range [2,4]: +2 at 2, -2 right after the range. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##7## Running total rebuilds the real array. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##8## One prefix pass. [for]({c:for})',
            '##9## Accumulate the diff into the current value. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##10## Prints the value at position `i`. [printf]({c:printf})',
            '##12## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: diffarray',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    int n = 5;',
            '    vector<int> d(n + 1, 0);',
            '    d[1] += 3; d[4] -= 3;',
            '    d[2] += 2; d[5] -= 2;',
            '    int cur = 0;',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {',
            '        cur += d[i];',
            '        cout << cur << " ";',
            '    }',
            '    cout << "\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## Array of 5 positions. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## Diff vector with one extra slot for the ending `-v`. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##6## Range [1,3]: +3 at 1, -3 right after the range. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##7## Range [2,4]: +2 at 2, -2 right after the range. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##8## Running total rebuilds the real array. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##9## One prefix pass. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/for)',
            '##10## Accumulate the diff into the current value. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##11## Prints the value at position `i`. [cout]({cpp:cout})',
            '##13## Success exit. [return](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return)',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: java',
            'group: diffarray',
            'import java.util.*;',
            'public class Main {',
            '    public static void main(String[] args) {',
            '        int n = 5;',
            '        int[] d = new int[6];',
            '        d[1] += 3; d[4] -= 3;',
            '        d[2] += 2; d[5] -= 2;',
            '        int cur = 0;',
            '        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {',
            '            cur += d[i];',
            '            System.out.print(cur + " ");',
            '        }',
            '        System.out.println();',
            '    }',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the `java.util` package. [import]({java:import})',
            '##2## In Java every function lives inside a class. [class]({java:class})',
