            '',
            '## Kadane\'s Algorithm',
            '',
            'Find the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray in one pass: extend the current run when it helps, restart when it hurts. O(n) time, O(1) space.',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: maxsubarray',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int a[] = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};',
            '    int n = 9;',
            '    int best = a[0], cur = a[0];',
            '    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {',
            '        cur = a[i] > cur + a[i] ? a[i] : cur + a[i];',
            '        if (cur > best) best = cur;',
            '    }',
            '    printf("%d\\n", best);',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## The input array. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##4## The array length. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## Best so far and current run, both start at `a[0]`. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##6## Start from the second element. [for]({c:for})',
            '##7## Restart at `a[i]` or extend the run. [if]({c:if})',
            '##8## Track the best run seen. [if]({c:if})',
            '##10## Prints the maximum subarray sum. [printf]({c:printf})',
            '##11## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: maxsubarray',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    vector<int> a = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};',
            '    int best = a[0], cur = a[0];',
            '    for (int i = 1; i < (int)a.size(); i++) {',
            '        cur = max(a[i], cur + a[i]);',
            '        best = max(best, cur);',
            '    }',
            '    cout << best << "\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##5## Best so far and current run, both start at `a[0]`. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##6## Start from the second element. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/for)',
            '##7## Restart at `a[i]` or extend the run. [max]({cpp:max})',
            '##8## Track the best run seen. [max]({cpp:max})',
            '##10## Prints the maximum subarray sum. [cout]({cpp:cout})',
            '##11## Success exit. [return](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return)',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: java',
            'group: maxsubarray',
            'import java.util.*;',
            'public class Main {',
            '    public static void main(String[] args) {',
            '        int[] a = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};',
