            '',
            '## Sliding Window Maximum Sum',
            '',
            'Keep a fixed-size window and slide it one step at a time: add the incoming element, subtract the outgoing one. O(n) for all window sums.',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: windowmax',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int a[] = {1, 4, 2, 10, 23, 3, 1, 0, 20};',
            '    int n = 9, k = 4;',
            '    int sum = 0, best;',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) sum += a[i];',
            '    best = sum;',
            '    for (int i = k; i < n; i++) {',
            '        sum += a[i] - a[i - k];',
            '        if (sum > best) best = sum;',
            '    }',
            '    printf("%d\\n", best);',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## The input array. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##4## Array length and window size. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## Window sum and the best seen so far. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##6## Seed the sum with the first window. [for]({c:for})',
            '##7## The first window is the initial best. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##8## Slide the window across the rest. [for]({c:for})',
            '##9## Add the incoming element, drop the outgoing one. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##10## Keep the best window. [if]({c:if})',
            '##12## Prints the maximum window sum. [printf]({c:printf})',
            '##13## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: windowmax',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    vector<int> a = {1, 4, 2, 10, 23, 3, 1, 0, 20};',
            '    int n = a.size(), k = 4;',
            '    int sum = 0, best;',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) sum += a[i];',
            '    best = sum;',
            '    for (int i = k; i < n; i++) {',
            '        sum += a[i] - a[i - k];',
            '        best = max(best, sum);',
            '    }',
            '    cout << best << "\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##5## Array length and window size. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##6## Window sum and the best seen so far. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##7## Seed the sum with the first window. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/for)',
            '##8## The first window is the initial best. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##9## Slide the window across the rest. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/for)',
            '##10## Add the incoming element, drop the outgoing one. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##11## Keep the best window. [max]({cpp:max})',
            '##13## Prints the maximum window sum. [cout]({cpp:cout})',
            '##14## Success exit. [return](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return)',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: java',
            'group: windowmax',
            'import java.util.*;',
            'public class Main {',
            '    public static void main(String[] args) {',
            '        int[] a = {1, 4, 2, 10, 23, 3, 1, 0, 20};',
            '        int n = a.length, k = 4;',
