            '',
            '## Two Pointers (Two Sum in a Sorted Array)',
            '',
            'With a sorted array, one pointer starts at the left, one at the right, and they move toward each other: too small, advance left; too large, move right. O(n) time, O(1) space.',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: twopointer',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int a[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6};',
            '    int n = 5, target = 6;',
            '    int i = 0, j = n - 1;',
            '    while (i < j) {',
            '        int s = a[i] + a[j];',
            '        if (s == target) {',
            '            printf("%d + %d = %d\\n", a[i], a[j], target);',
            '            return 0;',
            '        } else if (s < target) {',
            '            i++;',
            '        } else {',
            '            j--;',
            '        }',
            '    }',
            '    printf("no pair\\n");',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## Sorted input. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##4## Array length and the target sum. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## One pointer at each end. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##6## Stop when the pointers cross. [while]({c:while})',
            '##7## The current pair sum. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##8## Found the target. [if]({c:if})',
            '##9## Prints the pair and the target. [printf]({c:printf})',
            '##10## Exit immediately. [return]({c:return})',
            '##11## Too small → need a bigger sum. [if]({c:if})',
            '##12## Move the left pointer right. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##14## Too large → need a smaller sum. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##15## Move the right pointer left. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##17## No pair exists. [printf]({c:printf})',
            '##18## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: twopointer',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    vector<int> a = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6};',
            '    int target = 6;',
            '    int i = 0, j = (int)a.size() - 1;',
            '    while (i < j) {',
            '        int s = a[i] + a[j];',
            '        if (s == target) {',
            '            cout << a[i] << " + " << a[j] << " = " << target << "\\n";',
            '            return 0;',
            '        } else if (s < target) {',
            '            i++;',
            '        } else {',
            '            j--;',
            '        }',
            '    }',
            '    cout << "no pair\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## Sorted input. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##5## The target sum. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
            '##6## One pointer at each end. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##7## Stop when the pointers cross. [while](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/while)',
            '##8## The current pair sum. [Variables](https://www.learn-cpp.org/en/Variables)',
