            '',
            '## Frequency Counting',
            '',
            'Count how often each value appears. With small integer keys a plain array indexed by value is faster than a hash map: guaranteed O(1) per update.',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: c',
            'group: freqcount',
            '#include <stdio.h>',
            'int main() {',
            '    int a[] = {4, 2, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 4};',
            '    int n = 8;',
            '    int freq[100] = {0};',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) freq[a[i]]++;',
            '    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)',
            '        if (freq[i] > 0) printf("%d: %d\\n", i, freq[i]);',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Includes the standard input/output header so `printf` is available. [stdio]({c:stdio})',
            '##2## Every C program starts executing in `main()`. [main]({c:main})',
            '##3## The input array. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##4## The array length. [Variables](https://www.learn-c.org/en/Variables)',
            '##5## One counter slot per possible value. [Arrays]({c:array})',
            '##6## Increment the slot for each occurrence. [for]({c:for})',
            '##7## Walk the counter array. [for]({c:for})',
            '##8## Only print values that actually appear. [if]({c:if})',
            '##9## Success exit. [return]({c:return})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: cpp',
            'group: freqcount',
            '#include <bits/stdc++.h>',
            'using namespace std;',
            'int main() {',
            '    vector<int> a = {4, 2, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 4};',
            '    map<int, int> freq;',
            '    for (int x : a) freq[x]++;',
            '    for (auto& p : freq) cout << p.first << ": " << p.second << "\\n";',
            '    return 0;',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the whole C++ standard library. [bits/stdc++.h](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bitsstdc-h-c/)',
            '##2## Lets you write `cout` instead of `std::cout`. [namespace]({cpp:namespace})',
            '##3## Program entry point. [main]({cpp:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [vector]({cpp:vector})',
            '##5## `map` keys are kept sorted. [map](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/map)',
            '##6## Increment the count for each occurrence. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/range-for)',
            '##7## Print every key and its count. [for](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/range-for)',
            '##8## Success exit. [return](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return)',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: java',
            'group: freqcount',
            'import java.util.*;',
            'public class Main {',
            '    public static void main(String[] args) {',
            '        int[] a = {4, 2, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 4};',
            '        Map<Integer, Integer> freq = new TreeMap<>();',
            '        for (int x : a) freq.put(x, freq.getOrDefault(x, 0) + 1);',
            '        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> e : freq.entrySet())',
            '            System.out.println(e.getKey() + ": " + e.getValue());',
            '    }',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Imports the `java.util` package. [import]({java:import})',
            '##2## In Java every function lives inside a class. [class]({java:class})',
            '##3## `main` is where execution starts. [main]({java:main})',
            '##4## The input array. [Arrays](https://www.w3schools.com/java/java_arrays.asp)',
            '##5## `TreeMap` keeps keys sorted. [Map](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/Map.html)',
            '##6## `getOrDefault` treats a missing key as 0. [HashMap]({java:HashMap})',
            '##7## Iterate over the entries. [for]({java:for})',
            '##8## Print every key and its count. [println]({java:println})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: python',
            'group: freqcount',
            'def main():',
            '    a = [4, 2, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 4]',
            '    freq = {}',
            '    for x in a:',
            '        freq[x] = freq.get(x, 0) + 1',
            '    for k in sorted(freq):',
            '        print(k, ":", freq[k])',
            '',
            'if __name__ == "__main__":',
            '    main()',
            '---',
            '##1## Defines the main function. [def]({python:def})',
            '##2## The input array. [list]({python:list})',
            '##3## An empty dict for counts. [dict]({python:dict})',
            '##4## Count every occurrence. [for]({python:for})',
            '##5## `get(x, 0)` treats a missing key as 0. [dict]({python:dict})',
            '##6## Iterate keys in sorted order. [for]({python:for})',
            '##7## Print every key and its count. [print]({python:print})',
            '##9## Only runs when executed directly, not imported. [main]({python:main})',
            '##10## Calls `main()` so the program runs. [main]({python:main})',
            '~~~',
            '',
            '~~~explain',
            'lang: dart',
            'group: freqcount',
            'void main() {',
            '  var a = [4, 2, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 4];',
            '  var freq = <int, int>{};',
            '  for (var x in a) {',
            '    freq[x] = (freq[x] ?? 0) + 1;',
            '  }',
            '  var keys = freq.keys.toList()..sort();',
            '  for (var k in keys) {',
            '    print(\'$k: ${freq[k]}\');',
            '  }',
            '}',
            '---',
            '##1## Top-level entry point of a Dart program. [main]({dart:main})',
